      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s courthouse and jail, built in the 1800s, are on the National Register of Historic Places, reflecting its long civic history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newport%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Newport was platted in 1828 and has kept a post office running since 1820, showing its steady presence on the frontier.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newport%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every fall, the Newport Antique Auto Hill Climb draws over a hundred thousand visitors to race classic cars up the town’s 1,800‑foot hill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newport%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The historic walking tour in Newport highlights how residents helped runaway slaves escape via the Underground Railroad.",
